D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]silently losing whole relation classes.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]10[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]8[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]link_rail_every_tab.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]One projection for the machine-local read model[/bold #D7AFFF]               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]converge[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]converge: make every writer of `artifact-links.json` produce the same [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]row set, so the read model stops flapping by 233 rows an hour and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`cites`/`read` stop vanishing.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]A stale clone may not prove deletion[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]freshness[dim] · [dim][/dim]after converge[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]freshness: stop treating a companion file's mere existence as proof that[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]a row was deleted, so a behind-HEAD sidecar clone can no longer delete [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rows another workspace added.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Projected edges from facts SASE already owns[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]project[dim] · [dim][/dim]after converge[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]project: add a recomputed projection layer that turns commit trailers, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]agent metadata, and chop launch identity into typed edges without [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]growing the durable store.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]A way to read durable truth and see the drift[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]truthread[dim] · [dim][/dim]after converge, project[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]truthread: give the CLI and doctor a durable-truth read path and a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]row-level drift report, and build the harness that tests any index [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]against the store rather than against the aggregate.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]One selected-entity ref and one O(1) link index[/bold #D7AFFF]               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]subject[dim] · [dim][/dim]after truthread[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]subject: resolve the selected entity to a canonical ref on all three [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tabs and build the app-owned, alias-keyed edge index the render path [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reads with one dict lookup.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The Link Rail, read-only[/bold #D7AFFF]                                      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]rail[dim] · [dim][/dim]after subject[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]rail: mount the one-line, app-owned rail above the footer on every tab, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with the chip anatomy, stable ordering, degradation ladder, and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]invisibility contract.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The `$` grammar and a jump that always lands[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]follow[dim] · [dim][/dim]after rail[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]follow: bind `$` as a one-shot prefix for `$1`-`$9`/`$$`, gate it on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]availability, and make a cross-tab jump reveal, expand, and load [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]whatever it takes to land on the target.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Walking back across surfaces[/bold #D7AFFF]                                  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]trail[dim] · [dim][/dim]after follow[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]trail: add the app-level link trail and breadcrumb so [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`Ctrl+O`/`Ctrl+Shift+O` walk link hops across tabs and restore what a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]forward hop changed.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The `$0` Links panel[/bold #D7AFFF]                                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]panel[dim] · [dim][/dim]after follow[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]panel: build the overflow inspector that owns the long tail, the full [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`why`, provenance, the index-staleness notice, and the authoring verbs.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Retire the duplicates and land the rail[/bold #D7AFFF]                      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]land[dim] · [dim][/dim]after trail, panel[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]land: move link relations out of the pane relation panel, delete the two[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bespoke `L` jumps the rail generalizes, remove the flag, and verify the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]whole surface.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-ug","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-ug.4","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-a6b6038773deed729fddcb85182ab4f5","started_at":"2026-08-26T23:48:41.516340+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"9d1473391a6a0b63729d472850efcdbf32d